[KiCad-IOS port] Round 23: stage breadcrumbs on the two
dialog doors into the footprint chooser.

Sean's actual door (traced this round;
hidden_files/round23-bug-ledger.md): DIALOG_SYMBOL_PROPERTIES
is its own class, not the DIALOG_FIELD_PROPERTIES Round 22
traced. The button he taps is the wxGrid cell-editor control
TEXT_BUTTON_FP_CHOOSER (a wxComboCtrl) created by
GRID_CELL_FPID_EDITOR for the Footprint value cell; its
OnButtonClick (common/widgets/grid_text_button_helpers.cpp)
runs Player() -> KiwayMailIn -> ShowModal -> Destroy from
inside an ACTIVE grid edit session. Round 22's only caller-
side trace (round22-fpchooser-click) sits in the OTHER door
(dialog_field_properties.cpp), so Sean's path carried no
instrumentation at all.

This patch adds PATHS::IosBreadcrumb markers (patch 0054) to
BOTH doors with identical stage names, so whichever door Sean
uses, the log is readable the same way:
00-click (handler entry), 01-player-returned (the chooser
frame now exists -- everything before this line is Kiway /
kiface / constructor), 02-mail-done, 06-showmodal-enter,
07-showmodal-exit, 09-return-done (handler completed,
including Destroy). Read against the frame-side markers from
patch 0055, the last line in Documents/kicad-ios-breadcrumb.log
after a crash names the dying stage: e.g. 00 without 01 plus
10 without 14 = the constructor's guarded-Show span (ledger
#1); 16/17/18/06 present with 07 absent = inside the modal
loop (the kill-focus editor-dismissal suspect S1: the grid
editor's CallAfter(DisableCellEditControl) is executed by the
chooser's own event loop while OnButtonClick is still on the
stack); 07 present with 09 absent = the return path into the
dismissed editor (suspect S2). No behaviour changes: markers
only, all under KICAD_IOS_PORT.

Modified 2026-11-13 by the KiCad-IOS port (GPLv3 section 5
notice; see MODIFICATIONS.md).

